    "RegisterData[data] registers the data series. If data is 3D it performs \
multiple 2D registration, if data is 4D it performs multipe 3D registration. \
The target is the first image orvolume in the series.\nRegisterData[{data, \
vox}] registers the data series using the given voxel size.\n\
RegisterData[{data, mask}] registers the data series only using data whithin \
the mask.\nRegisterData[{data, mask, vox}] registers the data series using \
the given voxel size only using data within the mask.\n\nRegisterData[target, \
moving] registers the moving data to the target data. target can be 2D or 3D. \
moving can be the same of one dimension higher than the target.\n\
RegisterData[{target, mask, vox},{moving, mask, vox}] registers the data \
using the given voxel size only using data within the mask.\n\
RegisterData[{target, vox}, moving] registers the data using the given voxel \
size.\nRegisterData[target, {moving, vox}] registers the data using the given \
voxel size.\nRegisterData[{target, vox}, {moving, vox}] registers the data \
using the given voxel size.\n\nRegisterData[{target, mask}, moving] registers \
the data series only using data whithin the mask.\nRegisterData[target, \
{moving, mask}] registers the data series only using data whithin the mask.\n\
RegisterData[{target, mask}, moving] registers the data series only using \
data whithin the mask.\nRegisterData[{target, mask}, {moving, mask}] \
